:name: HWA10-logs
:description: Boot with readable wlog. Phase 0 gate.
# Shortcuts applied (see NOTES.md "Fidelity gaps"):
#  - sd_mbr_command (svc #24 @0x9301e) HardFaults under the emulated MBR; patched
#    to `movs r0,#0` so the thunk returns NRF_SUCCESS instead of faulting.
#  - the wlog ring producer blocks on semaphore 0xb2588 because its consumer
#    (an ISR/task that never runs without interrupts) does not drain it; that one
#    semaphore is forced non-blocking so logs flush.
#  - wlog is captured by hooking the ring putchar (0x56e8e) and printing bytes.

include @boot.resc

sysbus WriteWord 0x9301e 0x2000
cpu PerformanceInMips 200

cpu AddHook 0x3b4c0 """
if cpu.GetRegisterUnsafe(0).RawValue==0xb2588:
    b=cpu.GetMachine().SystemBus
    b.WriteDoubleWord(b.ReadDoubleWord(0xb2588)+0x11c, 1)
"""

cpu AddHook 0x56e8e """
g=globals()
c=cpu.GetRegisterUnsafe(0).RawValue & 0xff
buf=g.get('lb','')
if c==10:
    print 'WLOG| '+buf; g['lb']=''
else:
    buf=buf+(chr(c) if 32<=c<127 else '.')
    if len(buf)>=120: print 'WLOG> '+buf; buf=''
    g['lb']=buf
"""

emulation RunFor "0.2"
quit
